# Code of conduct

## The standard

Be civil. Assume the other person is acting in good faith, and argue about the
work rather than about them.

Unacceptable: harassment, personal attacks, demeaning comments, publishing
someone's private information, and sustained disruption of discussion.

This applies in issues, pull requests, commit messages, and any other project
space.

## Reporting

{% if coc_contact -%}
Report a violation to {{ coc_contact }}. Reports stay confidential.
{%- else -%}
Reports go to the maintainers. **Fill in a contact address here before publishing
this repository**: a code of conduct with no reporting channel asks people to
trust a process that does not exist.
{%- endif %}

## Enforcement

Maintainers may edit or remove a contribution, or block an account, for behaviour
they judge to breach the standard above. A first response is usually a private
warning.

